      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is understandable that you want the exhibit to celebrate pioneer grit, but framing displacement merely as a necessary side effect risks trivializing the profound suffering and systemic injustice that actually occurred. True historical accuracy requires honoring the indigenous people and their displacement with dignity before we can fully appreciate the complex legacy of the Westward Expansion. A powerful exhibit does not avoid difficult themes to preserve inspiration; rather, it gains its most lasting impact by telling the full, unvarnished story of who was moved, who stayed, and what was built upon that land.\n\nWould you be open to exploring a \"balanced narrative\" approach, where the exhibit pairs the spirit of discovery with a section that explicitly acknowledges the human cost without ending the overall tone on a negative note?",
